# Security policy

## Supported versions

Only the latest version, including betas, gets fixes.

## Reporting a vulnerability

Please report privately, never in a public issue. Use GitHub's
[Report a vulnerability](https://github.com/jasonaward/{{ repo }}/security/advisories/new)
(**Security** tab > **Advisories**). If you can't use GitHub, email
{{ public_email }}.

Include what you found, how to reproduce it, and the version. You can expect a reply
within a week. Please allow a reasonable time for a fix before disclosing it. Once a
vulnerability is fixed, it's published as a GitHub security advisory and noted in the
changelog.

## Scope

In scope: anything in this repository that could expose a user's credentials, tokens, or
private data (in logs, diagnostics, or elsewhere), or let someone else control a
{{ device }}.
{% if company %}
Out of scope: {{ company }}'s own service and app. Report those to {{ company }}.
{% endif %}
## What the integration does with your data

See [Security and privacy](README.md#security-and-privacy) in the README.

## Never post

Your password, tokens, `.storage` files, or recordings of network traffic. Diagnostics
downloads are designed to leave out private fields, but look them over before posting.
